  "Notes": "Single-wavelength AR at 1064 nm, two layers\n\nCaveats:\n- Manufacturability is scored with MINT/MAXT (minimum and maximum layer thickness) at a low weight. A sensitivity term (SENS) would score robustness to thickness errors directly, but it needs second derivatives of the merit function and is not offered; MINT/MAXT keep layers depositable and have exact derivatives.\n- L2 rather than minimax: with one wavelength there is nothing for a minimax to trade against, and the two norms coincide.",
